-- Cases for the seat layer sfab-seat.l4: up to three sets of facts a person in the seat could state for each question (the case that meets the provision, the case that does not,
-- and a case the text does not decide), with the answer written by hand from the text of the section the question names. The inputs are the layer-1 function's own, in the same order.


